whetstone (ccplugins) — sharpen the thinking before the work, and the work
before it lands.

Skills in this plugin are adapted, with modifications, from MIT-licensed prior
work:

  • mattpocock/skills (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock) — the `grilling`
    skill, the source of `/ws:grill`. The design-tree framing, the frontier
    (every decision whose prerequisites are settled), the round structure with
    the whole frontier asked at once, the ❓/➡️ question format with a
    recommended answer attached to every question, the facts-are-the-agent's /
    decisions-are-the-user's split, and the frontier-is-empty completion
    criterion all originate there.

  • openclaw/openclaw (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 OpenClaw Foundation) — the
    `test-audit` skill with its `CAMPAIGN.md`, and the `deslop` skill, from
    `.agents/skills/` at commit f61e10a7f49798cd7a041ca3509d3a2c5e0b99bc. The
    source of `/ws:test-gate`, `/ws:test-audit` (with
    `references/campaign.md`), `/ws:deslop`, and the shared
    `references/test-value.md`. The four authoring questions, the junk
    patterns, the value and retention bars, the candidate-evidence fields, the
    edit shape, the hand-off report, the eight-step campaign with its R/F/C/D
    ledger and mutation-checked preservation review, and the six-item slop
    checklist with its no-functional-edits rule all originate there.

Unlike a clean-room re-implementation, these are close textual adaptations: the
skills' prose derives from the originals and was rewritten, restructured and
extended rather than re-derived. Modifications are documented in CHANGELOG.md.
For `/ws:grill` they cover carrier selection (`AskUserQuestion` versus
markdown), the frontier-before-carrier ordering, enforced
non-consent-by-silence with an open list, and named hand-offs to the other
plugins in this marketplace. For the OpenClaw-derived skills they cover the
split of one three-mode skill into a model-invoked gate and a user-invoked
audit over a shared reference, an extend-don't-restructure rule that moves all
setup consolidation out of the gate, a notes file joining the two,
approval-before-edit in the audit and the campaign, additions for numerical
code, a diff scope for commit-to-main workflows, and the removal of every
OpenClaw-specific tool, path and flow.

